<title>POLAND: Polish shares end higher in continuous trade.</title>
<headline>Polish shares end higher in continuous trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine stocks rose, six fell and six were flat in 24.8-million-zloty Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Tuesday, with the WIG 20 index up 1.6 percent to 1,832.0 points.</p>
<p>Kety did not trade.</p>
<p>NFI units were flat at 163 zlotys in a 23.6-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
